set scriptsFolder to (path to library folder from user domain as string) & "Scripts:"set commonlib to load script alias (scriptsFolder & "Global.scpt")set spotifylib to load script alias (scriptsFolder & "Applications:Audio Hijack Pro:Spotify.scpt")try	tell application "Audio Hijack Pro"		activate		set theSession to first session whose name is "Spotify" --By name				stop recording theSession	end tellon error	display dialog "Start Spotify: Could not connect to Audio Hijack Pro, stopping script"	returnend trytry	tell application "Spotify"		activate		set sound volume to 100		-- start then stop to set current track		playSpotify() of spotifylib		skipDuplicate() of spotifylib		stopSpotify() of spotifylib		try			tell current track				get id			end tell		on error errMsg number errNum			display dialog "Start Spotify: Doesn't seem to be a current track, select a playlist and a track to start" & errMsg			return		end try		tell current track			-- get current track data			set theTitle to name			set theArtist to artist			set theAlbum to album			set theDuration to duration		end tell		playSpotify() of spotifylib		delay 5		rewindSpotify() of spotifylib		try			tell application "Audio Hijack Pro"				-- setup Hijack tags				set theSession to first session whose name is "Spotify" --By name 				set title tag of theSession to theTitle				set album tag of theSession to theAlbum				set artist tag of theSession to theArtist				set silence monitor action of theSession to {action:stop, duration:1.5, level:-60.0}				start recording theSession			end tell					on error errMsg number errNum			display dialog "Start Spotify: Could not start recording session, stopping script. " & errMsg			return		end try	end tellon error errMsg number errNum	display dialog "Start Spotify: Can connect to Spotify, stopping script. " & errMsgend try